    "name": "Air Fryer Japanese Fried Chicken (Karaage)",
    "description": "Crispy, juicy Japanese fried chicken made in the air fryer. The double-fry technique — low heat first, then high heat — gives the signature crunchy exterior while keeping the meat tender inside.",
    "recipeCategory": {
      "_id": "6a4dc38cf8d89f9a72f510c9",
      "name": "Protein",
      "normalizedName": "protein",
      "isDefault": false,
      "isArchived": false,
      "createdAt": "2026-07-08T03:27:08.972Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-08T03:27:08.972Z",
      "__v": 0
    },
    "mealCategory": [
      "dinner",
      "lunch"
    ],
    "servings": 4,
    "defaultPortionUnit": "serving",
    "nutritionBasis": "per-serving",
    "imageUrl": "",
    "notes": "Marinate for at least 30 min (up to 1 hour). Potato starch (katakuriko) gives the crispiest coating — use cornstarch as a substitute. Serve with lemon wedges.",
    "isArchived": true,
